1. Added the ScopeProvider import from the scope context
2. Added RouterContext from Next.js since ScopeProvider requires router context
3. Created a mock router object with the necessary properties that ScopeProvider needs
4. Wrapped the component with both RouterContext.Provider and ScopeProvider

The component structure remains exactly the same, we've just added the necessary providers that the PostComposer component needs to function properly. The mock router provides the minimum required context for the ScopeProvider to work correctly.

